{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Pre-sweep against `origin/main` `757ca4852d7`, before spending a gate slot\n\nOne defect fixed, and the plan's Testing section re-verified in full.\n\n### Defect: `file_impact` still named ADR 0119\n\nThe description moved the consolidated record to **0121** (because 0119 and 0120 were both taken by the MCP-surface and CLI-verb ADRs), but `file_impact` still listed `docs/adr/0119-reconciler-architecture-consolidated-record.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/0119`. That matters beyond tidiness: `file_impact` is this ticket's `currency_basis`, and the completion gate's precheck reads it, so the close would have been checked against 2 paths the implementation never creates. Both entries are now repointed to 0121; the other 21 were already correct.\n\n### 0121 is still the right number, re-measured\n\n`ls docs/adr/.numbers | sort | tail` gives `0117 0118 0119 0120` — 0120 is the highest taken and **0121 is free**. All 20 originals named in the plan are present on `757ca4852d7`.\n\n### Testing section re-verified, every citation\n\n| Citation | State at `757ca4852d7` |\n|---|---|\n| 5 cited scripts (`check_adr_numbers`, `gen_adr_index`, `check_docs_index`, `check_criteria_vocabulary`, `check_dco_identity`) | all present |\n| `test_wiki_render.py::test_adr_0095_records_the_required_sections` | present, **`:329`** — the exact line the plan cites |\n| the 0095 body pin | **`:338`** — the exact line the plan cites |\n| `test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py::test_default_context_routes_summary_only_update_through_legacy` | present, `:45` |\n| `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py`, `test_check_adr_numbers.py`, `test_gerrit_docs_only.py` | all present |\n\nThe earlier pre-sweep corrected these against `d74d53a5ffd`; they have not drifted since.\n\n### Cross-story check: the one shared file\n\n`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` is cited here and also edited by sibling story `fb5f-54fd-96cc-4105`, which is merging 17 held-out twin pairs under `tests/interfaces/`. Checked directly against that story's working tree: `fb5f` **modifies** the file (2 allowlist rows) and does **not** delete it — it is not in `fb5f`'s pair list. This Testing target survives either landing order.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793494499606669628,"uuid":"6557465c-c599-44a3-b801-3e569fa9373a"}